# Tesla Dashboard: environment template
# Copy to .env for local development (`npm start` runs netlify dev, which reads
# .env). Deployed sites use Netlify > Site configuration > Environment variables:
# set each secret with scope "Functions", mark it "Contains secret values", and
# give it a value in every deploy context.

# ── Server-side secrets (Netlify Functions only) ────────────────────────────
# Never prefix a secret with VITE_: Vite builds every VITE_* value into the
# public JavaScript bundle.

# OpenWeather: weather + zip lookup (https://openweathermap.org/api)
OPENWEATHER_API_KEY=your_openweather_api_key_here

# Geoapify: Places tab + address search (https://myprojects.geoapify.com/)
GEOAPIFY_API_KEY=your_geoapify_api_key_here

# TomTom: traffic incidents + drive times; key needs the Traffic API and
# Routing API enabled (https://developer.tomtom.com/)
TOMTOM_API_KEY=your_tomtom_api_key_here

# ── Public build-time settings (safe to expose) ─────────────────────────────
# Fallback location when GPS is unavailable (Boston)
VITE_DEFAULT_LAT=42.364506
VITE_DEFAULT_LON=-71.038887

# News needs no key: /api/news reads free public RSS feeds.
